8.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Odd | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/3ae81378cb3c918dd5b7730519eb5a91e949f88eef9f03f4910f4ab8fb3cd5a9.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/9506a7ce4031f1f6244c0110c3235f66ea5652bb53548a032732869cf21f5997.png) |\n\nIt's possible to determine information regarding the multiplicities of the roots of a polynomial from its graph.\n\n- If the graph intersects the $x$-axis but is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *simple* root $x=a.$\n\n- If the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *multiple* root $x=a.$ Furthermore:\n\n- If the graph touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *even*.\n\n- If the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *odd*.\n\nIn our case, the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=-1.$ So, $x=-1$ is a *multiple* root. \n\nFurthermore, the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=-1.$ So, $x=-1$ has *odd* multiplicity.\n\nTherefore, $x=-1$ is a multiple root of odd multiplicity." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141133/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d48e2a0-1a76-5eec-a98c-4a7eb16f70cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141133"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141144/selection/bfca0602accb030faa6043daee9f29938ae13b8cdf24ed13910812df5c38e3cd" :answer/id #uuid "679e573a-c099-5325-b53f-a8b1dc965f86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=6$ is a simple root" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141144/selection/806f0db2ee3d059b4ce7d3b93c630846113c0134cc76948bad6cecf1aa0c792b" :answer/id #uuid "555077fb-711f-5f11-929e-2520a27f8729" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=6$ is not a root of $p(x)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141144/select