97.png) |\n\nIt's possible to determine information regarding the multiplicities of the roots of a polynomial from its graph.\n\n- If the graph intersects the $x$-axis but is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *simple* root $x=a.$\n\n- If the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *multiple* root $x=a.$ Furthermore:\n\n- If the graph touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *even*.\n\n- If the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *odd*.\n\nIn our case, the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=-5.$ So, $x=-5$ is a *multiple* root. \n\nFurthermore, the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=-5.$ So, $x=-5$ has *odd* multiplicity.\n\nTherefore, $x=-5$ is a multiple root of odd multiplicity." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141137/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d48e2a0-1a76-5eec-a98c-4a7eb16f70cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141137"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141142/selection/534ad9f75ac5322389d40b0d860d84ba95541626f1fde2d8030c10f3b068eb1d" :answer/id #uuid "2cf05d42-31cc-534e-b1bc-1a57738ff8d5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=9$ is a multiple root of odd multiplicity" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141142/selection/1f129670aff730e6f4bcbb3ab4ebf237971d0a72934442772a8918f24af4305c" :answer/id #uuid "47e60bb5-42a1-5be2-bebc-f6ae7701aac1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=9$ is not a root of $p(x)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141142/selection/5fab14017b1faa6d0509affd91ada53c5a3a530f61676a4aad157b972e7c96c6" :answer/id #uuid "20eba10d-304b-5e19-8b73-cbed3f711997" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=9$ is a simple root of even multiplicity" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141142/selection/af826042215c706a6729ccd11ee02e44f6ec5b1256480e1706d3624249d4b31d" :answer/i