tion/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/5e4e2241490626139e15800f3b90c8e15a9963bdcace9907f8557b0897d533e6.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $p(0)$ is positive.\n- $p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n- $x=0$ is a root of odd multiplicity." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The graph passes through the $y$-axis at $y=0,$ which means that $p(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves down in the negative direction towards $-\\infty .$\n\n- Statement III is true. The root $x=0$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112585/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80303/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d35f02c4-7983-53d4-9166-a7b112563ba8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80303/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "b5ef9e97-aa7f-5815-b914-486e751f3282" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80303/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "ad4d25ba-c0bc-513e-bfb6-861b79a5f728" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80303/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "f7c69bde-0ca6-54c8-8c29-ec7723099a86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80303/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "13aba830-b445-5607-bfb3-d276b38f0ff0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80303/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "50c528ef-945c-5b58-bf6a-8a7b821c6038" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80303/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-80303/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-80303/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-80303/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-80303/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-80303/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80303" :question/id #uuid "91d3ac9b-2d2d-5160-bd5c-1e34a396139a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80303" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/0a7b19b50822235a2dcbfcdf74984735a1e26b2b775180b24bdc2bcbf24c588b.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=-2$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n- $x=1$ is **not** a simple root.\n- $x=1$ is a root of even multiplicity." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The root $x=-2$ has an odd multiplicity because at $x=-2$ the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=1$ is not a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at that point, and the curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement III is false. The root $x=1$ has an odd multiplicity because at $x=1$ the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80303/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80303"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-38680/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "a84e8d3d-325f-55fb-be6f-c332072f47ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38680/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "20d36a72-f50d-5f0c-b0fe-8dfca7aa7246" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38680/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "760d168b-bd98-548a-9e1a-836ac1db5d5d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38680/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "c421830f-d672-591f-936f-7841571e829e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38680/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "4b1ff5c9-ae03-5578-886d-cf9c77888723" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38680/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ac26998-6f00-53e0-a2de-939d74eed232" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38680/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices