ecause at $x=2$ the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Statement III is false. The root $x=2$ is not a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at that point, and the curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80302/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80302"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112595/selection/d2812d4caf4ac0978eafbed1dae7758359cb4dfb17894e11f20daf56d207957c" :answer/id #uuid "30e7684e-ed73-54c7-b84f-f37ab5d39d56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{2}(x+3)(x-2{)}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112595/selection/6a9471c899827144c908f40026e903c483ded5a3c9e09f7faec7663da8142641" :answer/id #uuid "49b52793-e35b-5508-a471-d141859af4fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-3x(x+3)(x-2{)}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112595/selection/6f74109d45667fd683acf3cf30b48538ab8a59ac03029b7a377450872d435c23" :answer/id #uuid "bd3f89a2-5e94-570b-9a18-c7dd0f9c4ef9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{x}^{4}(x-3{)}^{3}(x-2{)}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112595/selection/58926a3c120a4943dfcdd0d3a49be676943cbd099d2353f750d10d09c1fd9a64" :answer/id #uuid "ef6048d7-b982-53a8-975e-716c88a2f3a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-8{x}^{4}(x+3)(x-2{)}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112595/selection/04ecc1fa62e5fc293a6be20c9eccf1e96d01baa6da51f59f1cd4af269d22512e" :answer/id #uuid "26d4c130-8b5a-5e05-a48f-6d4bea3a5507" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{5}x(x-3)(x-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112595/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "35baf619-5f20-5233-affa-5a93ab407e0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-f